# Always Bump the Page Version on Every Change

These pages are cached aggressively. Whenever you make ANY functional change to a
file in `team/`, you MUST bump BOTH version markers so the team can visually confirm
the new code is live. Never leave them stale.

## 1. The visible banner version (`PAGE_VERSION`)

This is displayed to users in the on-page version banner. Increment it every change.

```js
// ❌ BAD — left unchanged after editing behavior
const PAGE_VERSION = 'v2.10.0-shared-pool';

// ✅ GOOD — bumped with a short suffix describing the change
const PAGE_VERSION = 'v2.10.1-queue-sort-fix';
```

Use semver-ish bumps: patch (`v2.10.0` → `v2.10.1`) for fixes/tweaks, minor
(`v2.10.x` → `v2.11.0`) for behavior changes. Keep the short `-kebab-suffix`.

## 2. The HTML cache-buster comment (top of `<head>`)

```html
<!-- CACHE BUSTER v4.12.0 - SHARED POOL: ... -->
```

Bump this version too and update its note to describe what changed.

## Checklist before finishing any edit to `team/**/*.html`

- [ ] `PAGE_VERSION` incremented
- [ ] `<!-- CACHE BUSTER vX.Y.Z ... -->` incremented + note updated
- [ ] Any on-page banner text that describes behavior still matches reality
